 {
  "id": "art-0023-southeast-asia-haze-2026",
  "slug": "southeast-asia-haze-johor-schools-singapore-2026",
  "headline": "Haze Chokes Southeast Asia: Johor Schools Shut Until Oct 16, Singapore Air Stays Unhealthy",
  "socialHeadline": "Johor extended school closures to Oct 16 and Singapore's air stayed unhealthy as smoke from Indonesian fires drifts across the region",
  "summary": "Johor state extended school closures to October 16 and Singapore's air quality remained in the unhealthy range as smoke haze from fires in Indonesia's Sumatra and Kalimantan drifted across Southeast Asia.",
  "body": [
   "The Malaysian state of Johor extended the closure of all schools and educational institutions by five more days, through October 16, 2026, as haze worsened across the region. The announcement was made late Saturday, October 10, by state education and information committee chairman Muhammad Naqib Md Ghazali, by decree of the Regent of Johor, Tunku Mahkota Ismail.",
   "The extension follows a statewide closure on October 8-9 and affects 1,198 schools and 617,258 students, according to The Star. Students will continue home-based learning and scheduled assessments have been postponed. Officials cited forecasts that winds from Indonesia's Kalimantan between October 13 and 15 could bring more transboundary pollution; 15 areas in Malaysia recorded unhealthy Air Pollutant Index readings on Sunday morning, eight of them in Johor.",
   "In Singapore, air quality remained in the unhealthy range across all five regions on October 11. The National Environment Agency said the 24-hour PSI ranged from 115 to 152 as of 9am Sunday, after the central region hit 192 on Friday evening \u2014 a season high \u2014 and warned the index could exceed 200, the 'very unhealthy' threshold. The haze comes from smoke drifting on east-southeasterly winds from southern Sumatra and Kalimantan. A 28-agency Haze Task Force has been convened, and the Formula 1 Singapore Grand Prix weekend is proceeding with contingency measures in place.",
   "## Why it matters",
   "The annual transboundary haze season is again disrupting daily life across the region, with authorities in both countries warning conditions could deteriorate further in the coming days."
  ],
  "category": "World",
  "tags": [
