 {
  "id": "art-0027-singapore-sparkletots-20-million-2026",
  "slug": "singapore-pcf-sparkletots-staff-training-20-million-2027",
  "headline": "Singapore's Largest Preschool Operator to Double Teacher Training Spend to S$20 Million",
  "socialHeadline": "PCF Sparkletots will invest S$20 million in staff development over three years from 2027 and offer Chinese, Malay and Tamil in all its preschools \u2014 announced at its 40th anniversary celebrations",
  "summary": "Singapore's largest preschool operator, PCF Sparkletots, will double its investment in staff development to S$20 million over three years from 2027, the organization announced on Sunday at a family day event at Mandai Wildlife Reserve marking its 40th anniversary.",
  "body": [
   "PCF Sparkletots, Singapore's largest preschool operator, will double what it spends on training its teachers to S$20 million over the next three years, the PAP Community Foundation (PCF) announced on Sunday at a family day event at Mandai Wildlife Reserve celebrating the foundation's 40th anniversary.",
   "The investment will begin from 2027 and goes alongside a plan to offer Chinese, Malay and Tamil in all its preschools from 2027 where there is demand, plus an enhanced centralized model to cut administrative work across its centres so educators can spend more time with children and teaching.",
   "## Four decades of PCF",
   "Deputy Prime Minister Gan Kim Yong, who attended as guest of honour, said PCF had over 40 years supported more than a million children, served some 30,000 seniors, and empowered more than 46,000 vulnerable beneficiaries.",
   "PCF today operates close to 350 preschool centres, making it Singapore's largest preschool operator. It is also the country's third-largest senior care provider, with 11 senior care centres and nine active ageing centres.",
   "## Why teachers matter",
   "PCF Council of Management chairperson Josephine Teo, who is also Singapore's Minister for Digital Development and Information, said the investment reflected the outsized role teachers play in children's learning: parents entrust the operator with their children's formative years, so it must develop its teachers to help them be more effective and give every child a strong start.",
   "The announcement fits a longer shift in Singapore's early childhood sector, where anchor operators like PCF Sparkletots have moved from simply expanding centre numbers to upgrading teacher quality and curriculum \u2014 a direction the Early Childhood Development Agency has encouraged to keep fees affordable while raising standards."
  ],
  "category": "World",
  "tags": [
   "Singapore",
   "Education",
   "Preschool",
   "PCF Sparkletots",
   "Asia"
  ],
  "author": "NewsVeria Newsroom",
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-11T10:21:25Z",
  "image": {
   "src": "/images/media-generation-nv-sparkletots-preschool-0-0-fba64f7b-c021-42c6-bf6b-c3abbb8bcde0.webp",
   "alt": "Flat illustration of a preschool classroom with a teacher and faceless geometric children, crayons and blocks",
   "caption": "Illustration: NewsVeria generated editorial illustration. NewsVeria uses clearly labelled generated illustrations and never presents imagery as real event photography.",
   "credit": "NewsVeria generated illustration"
  },
