 {
  "author": "NewsVeria Newsroom",
  "body": [
   "Pope Leo XIV announced on Sunday that he will undergo surgery this week after doctors discovered a nodule on his lung, telling thousands gathered in St Peter's Square for the weekly Angelus that the growth was detected at what he described as a very early stage.",
   "The 71-year-old pontiff said his doctors had recommended the operation and that he had decided to go ahead with it, asking the crowd for their prayers. The announcement, made in person from the window of the Apostolic Palace, was his first public disclosure of a health issue since his election.",
   "Vatican spokesman Matteo Bruni confirmed that the surgery is scheduled for the first days of the week and is expected to take place at Rome's Gemelli Hospital, the facility that has treated popes for decades. Recovery is expected to take about a week, the Vatican said.",
   "Officials stressed that the nodule is localized and was caught early. The pope, who turned 71 this year, has had no previously known health problems during his pontificate.",
   "The announcement raises questions about the pope's upcoming travel plans, including a scheduled trip to Latin America from November 6 to 17. The Vatican has not said whether the itinerary will be affected.",
   "The news drew immediate reaction from Catholic leaders and heads of state, with messages of support arriving from around the world within hours of the Angelus address."
  ],
