  "body": [
   "The United States on Friday imposed sweeping sanctions on the International Criminal Court, targeting the tribunal as an institution in a dramatic escalation of Washington's campaign against it.",
   "Secretary of State Marco Rubio announced the measures, saying the administration would \"ban transactions with this rogue court, cutting off their resources and crippling its ability to operate against us.\" Under the sanctions, the court's assets in US jurisdictions are blocked, and American entities have been given a six-month wind-down period to sever ties, with exemptions for telecommunications, software, pensions and transactions involving detainees.",
   "The court in The Hague condemned the move as \"an assault on the rule of law and on the very foundations of the international legal order,\" and called on its 125 member states to defend the institution.",
   "The announcement came just hours after former ICC judge Navi Pillay was awarded the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize \u2014 a juxtaposition that drew immediate international attention. The measures go far beyond earlier US sanctions, which had targeted 17 individual ICC judges and officials; this is the first time the court itself has been sanctioned as an entity. US allies including Britain, Canada, Denmark, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the Netherlands issued statements of regret, and UN Secretary-General Ant\u00f3nio Guterres called the move a \"serious blow.\""
  ],
