 {
  "author": "NewsVeria Newsroom",
  "body": [
   "Donald Trump lashed out at Norway late on Friday after the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize was awarded to South African jurist Navi Pillay, calling the committee's decision an \"indelible stain on the country of Norway.\"",
   "Speaking at a rally in Syracuse, New York, Trump described the award as a \"disgraceful and embarrassing decision\" and said the Norwegian Nobel Committee had been \"forever discredited.\" He told the crowd he had never heard of this year's winner. In a roughly 600-word post on Truth Social, he claimed he had \"settled eight wars\" and deserved the prize himself.",
   "The laureate, 85-year-old Navi Pillay, is a South African jurist who served as a judge of the International Criminal Court and as the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights. Accepting the honour, she quipped: \"If you clap a little bit more, I may share this prize with Trump.\"",
   "The prize was announced on Friday morning in Oslo. Trump has campaigned openly for the Nobel Peace Prize for years, repeatedly listing conflicts he says his diplomacy helped end \u2014 claims that fact-checkers have disputed."
  ],
  "breaking": false,
  "category": "World",
