  "body": [
   "Eliud Kipchoge ended a three-year wait for a marathon victory in emphatic fashion on Sunday, winning the Melbourne Marathon in a course-record 2:09:10.",
   "The 41-year-old Kenyan broke away from the field inside the final 10 kilometres and crossed the line two seconds inside the previous race record of 2:09:12, set by Timothy Ronoh in 2022. It was Kipchoge's 17th career marathon victory \u2014 and his first since Berlin in September 2023.",
   "The race, which began at 6:15 a.m. local time, finished with a half-lap inside the Melbourne Cricket Ground, where Kipchoge soaked in the applause of the home crowd.",
   "Australia's Thomas Do Canto finished second in 2:10:35, with compatriot Reece Edwards third in 2:14:33. New Zealand's Camille French won the women's race in 2:28:25. For Kipchoge, the two-time Olympic champion widely regarded as the greatest marathoner in history, the win marks a striking late-career resurgence at 41."
  ],
  "breaking": false,
  "category": "Sports",
