 {
  "id": "art-0037-greenlaw-ejection-49ers-seahawks-2026",
  "slug": "greenlaw-ejected-head-butt-seahawks-32-29",
  "headline": "Dre Greenlaw Ejected for Head-Butting Helmetless Ernest Jones IV as 49ers Edge Seahawks 32-29",
  "socialHeadline": "The 49ers linebacker was disqualified in the second quarter after a late hit on Sam Darnold and a head-butt on a helmetless Ernest Jones IV \u2014 but San Francisco stayed unbeaten with a 32-29 win in Seattle",
  "summary": "San Francisco stayed undefeated with a 32-29 win over Seattle on Sunday, but lost linebacker Dre Greenlaw to a second-quarter ejection after a late hit on Sam Darnold was followed by a head-butt on helmetless Seahawks linebacker Ernest Jones IV. Seattle committed four turnovers.",
  "body": [
   "The San Francisco 49ers survived their own linebacker's temper on Sunday, beating the Seattle Seahawks 32-29 at Lumen Field to remain undefeated \u2014 despite losing Dre Greenlaw to an ejection midway through the second quarter.",
   "The sequence began with a late hit by Greenlaw on Seahawks quarterback Sam Darnold near the sideline, which drew an unnecessary-roughness flag. As pushing and shoving broke out on the Seattle sideline, Greenlaw \u2014 still wearing his helmet \u2014 head-butted Seahawks linebacker Ernest Jones IV, who was not wearing his. Officials disqualified Greenlaw from the game, ending his afternoon.",
   "The ejection could easily have tilted the NFC West showdown toward Seattle. Instead, San Francisco's defense forced four turnovers. A fumble at the goal line recovered in the end zone by rookie defensive tackle Gracen Halton just before halftime gave the 49ers a 21-13 lead they would not surrender.",
   "Seattle fought back: Jaxon Smith-Njigba's 16-yard touchdown put the Seahawks ahead 23-21 in the third quarter, and Jason Myers' kicking kept it close late. But the 49ers' takeaways proved decisive in the 32-29 final.",
   "Greenlaw's ejection adds to a heated chapter of the 49ers-Seahawks rivalry. No suspension had been announced as of publication, and this story makes no claim about further league discipline."
  ],
  "category": "Sports",
  "tags": [
   "NFL",
