 {
  "id": "art-0038-packers-bears-burden-quit-2026",
  "slug": "packers-beat-bears-31-7-burden-quit",
  "headline": "Packers Maul Bears 31-7, Then Fire Back at Luther Burden III: 'He Quit'",
  "socialHeadline": "Green Bay backed up its pregame talk with a 31-7 rout at Lambeau, then answered Bears receiver Luther Burden III's 'make them quit' vow \u2014 as Chicago played without injured Caleb Williams",
  "summary": "The Green Bay Packers thrashed the Chicago Bears 31-7 at Lambeau Field on Sunday, then delivered the verbal knockout. Linebacker Zaire Franklin fired back at Bears receiver Luther Burden III, who had promised before the game to 'beat them real bad and make them quit' \u2014 'He quit today,' Franklin said. Chicago played without injured quarterback Caleb Williams.",
  "body": [
   "The talking started before kickoff. Chicago Bears receiver Luther Burden III vowed his team would \"beat them real bad and make them quit\" when the Bears visited Lambeau Field on Sunday. The Green Bay Packers heard it \u2014 and made the trash talk their motivation in a 31-7 Week 5 rout on October 11, 2026.",
   "After the game, Packers linebacker Zaire Franklin delivered the rebuttal. \"He quit today,\" Franklin said of Burden, turning the receiver's own vow back on him after Green Bay dominated in all phases.",
   "The Bears were also shorthanded where it mattered most. With starting quarterback Caleb Williams injured, Chicago turned to backup Tyson Bagent, and the offense never found its rhythm against a Packers defense that fed off the home crowd.",
   "The 31-7 final was a statement in the NFC North's oldest rivalry \u2014 and a reminder that pregame guarantees only count if you back them up. Burden and the Bears learned that lesson the hard way at Lambeau."
  ],
