 {
  "id": "art-0040-mendoza-nfl-debut-raiders-2026",
  "slug": "fernando-mendoza-nfl-debut-raiders-patriots",
  "headline": "No. 1 Pick Fernando Mendoza Makes NFL Debut in Raiders' 45-17 Loss to Patriots",
  "socialHeadline": "The 2026 top draft pick entered late at Gillette Stadium, going 6-of-8 for 48 yards in mop-up duty. Coach Klint Kubiak: 'He did a good job.'",
  "summary": "The 2026 No. 1 overall pick is officially an NFL quarterback. Fernando Mendoza made his regular-season debut for the Las Vegas Raiders on Sunday, entering late in a 45-17 loss to the New England Patriots at Gillette Stadium. The rookie completed 6 of 8 passes for 48 yards, and coach Klint Kubiak praised his first outing.",
  "body": [
   "It came in garbage time, but it was history. With about six minutes left on Sunday and the Las Vegas Raiders trailing the New England Patriots 45-17 at Gillette Stadium, the 2026 No. 1 overall pick jogged onto the field for his first NFL regular-season action.",
   "Fernando Mendoza, the Raiders' franchise hope from the 2026 draft, operated the offense calmly in his brief stint, completing 6 of 8 passes for 48 yards against a Patriots defense protecting a 28-point lead.",
   "Head coach Klint Kubiak liked what he saw. \"He did a good job,\" Kubiak said of the rookie's first taste of NFL speed.",
   "The result itself was never in doubt \u2014 the Patriots controlled the Week 5 game throughout on October 11. But for Raiders fans, the scoreline was secondary. The debut of the No. 1 pick, however brief, was the moment that mattered, and Mendoza now has his first NFL snaps in the books."
  ],
